### Synapse MinimalApi — Streaming (IStreamRequest<T>)
### Demonstrates: IStreamRequest<T>, IAsyncEnumerable yielded items, StreamLoggingBehavior.
### Run `dotnet run` in examples/MinimalApi, then execute requests top-to-bottom.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5225

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Setup — create a couple of tasks so the stream has something to yield
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Create task 1
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Stream task Alpha",
  "description": "First task for the streaming demo"
}

> {%
    client.test("Task Alpha created", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 201, "Expected 201 Created");
    });
%}

###

### Create task 2
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Stream task Beta",
  "description": "Second task for the streaming demo"
}

> {%
    client.test("Task Beta created", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 201, "Expected 201 Created");
    });
%}

###

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Streaming request
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### [Feature: IStreamRequest<T>] Stream all tasks as IAsyncEnumerable
### The handler yields each TaskDto one by one; ASP.NET Core flushes them as a JSON array.
###
### Observe stdout (StreamLoggingBehavior):
###   "🔢 Streamed N StreamTasksQuery item(s) in <elapsed>"
###
### This log line appears AFTER the stream completes — the behavior wraps the
### IAsyncEnumerable from next() and counts items as they are yielded.
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/stream
Accept: application/json

> {%
    client.test("Stream endpoint returns 200", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected 200 OK");
        client.assert(Array.isArray(response.body), "Response is an array");
        client.assert(response.body.length >= 2, "At least 2 tasks streamed");
    });

    client.test("Each item has the expected shape", function () {
        const first = response.body[0];
        client.assert(first.id !== undefined, "id present");
        client.assert(first.title !== undefined, "title present");
        client.assert(first.status !== undefined, "status present");
    });
%}

###
